# Accessibility (a11y)

WCAG 2.2 AA intent. Prefer semantic HTML over `aria-*` patches.

- Use real controls (`button`, `a`, `label`, landmarks, headings) — no `div`/`span` click handlers for actions
- Every interactive control has an accessible **name** (visible text, `aria-label`, or labelled-by)
- Icons-only buttons: `aria-label` (translate it); decorative icons: `aria-hidden`
- Forms: associate labels and errors (`htmlFor`, `aria-describedby`, `aria-invalid`)
- Keyboard: Tab/Enter/Space/Escape parity; visible focus; no traps
- Dialogs/menus: use shadcn/Radix when possible (focus management built-in)
- Don’t rely on color alone for meaning
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` for non-essential animation
- Tests: prefer `getByRole` + name

Details: `docs/frontend/conventions/ACCESSIBILITY.md`
